ready: 1
kind: sequence
id: stacks.seq.daemon-start
display_id: SEQ-STACKS-DAEMON
module: stacks
title: Start the daemon and catch up
summary: Takes the home's single-daemon lock, opens every stack, catches up missed work, and then serves
  requests.
trigger:
  trigger_kind: event
  text: The service manager starts the daemon at login or boot, after init, or when the owner starts it
operation: stacks.op.daemon
participants:
- id: services
  label: OS service manager
- sys.daemon
- sys.home
items:
- msg:
    from: services
    to: sys.daemon
    text: Start
    owner: crates/kernled/src/main.rs::run
- msg:
    from: sys.daemon
    to: sys.home
    text: Take the home's exclusive daemon lock
    ops:
    - op: lock
      path: ~/.kernle/run/kernled.lock
      mode: exclusive
- alt:
    branches:
    - when: another daemon holds the lock
      items:
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: services
          text: Exit and leave the running daemon in charge
          reply: true
    - when: the lock is acquired
      items:
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: sys.home
          text: Open the registry and each stack database at this binary's schema
          ops:
          - op: read
            entity: stacks.data.stack
            by:
            - every row
      - opt:
          when: a stack database cannot be opened, or is newer than this binary
          items:
          - note:
              over:
              - sys.daemon
              text: Mark that stack unavailable for this run, leave its files untouched, and show it in
                status
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: sys.daemon
          text: Ingest transcript records added since each source's cursor
          invokes:
          - capture.seq.ingest
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: sys.daemon
          text: Bring each stack's search index up to date
          invokes:
          - recall.seq.index
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: sys.daemon
          text: Start the scheduler, which runs any retention or sleep that was missed
          invokes:
          - consolidation.seq.schedule
      - msg:
          from: sys.daemon
          to: sys.home
          text: Listen on the owner-only socket
          constants:
          - stacks.const.file-modes
          ops:
          - op: write
            path: ~/.kernle/run/kernled.sock
rationale: One daemon per home, enforced with a file lock, because two daemons would be two writers to
  every stack database. Catch-up at start lets a stopped daemon delay memory without losing it, since
  the runtimes keep their transcripts. A stack that cannot be upgraded stays untouched and visible, because
  repairing it automatically could destroy memory.
